<section class="page-section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <aside class="split__aside">
      <span class="eyebrow">I / Design</span>
      <h2>One line, held.</h2>
    </aside>
    <div class="split__body" data-reveal>
      <p>
        The visual system is an editorial grid with an engraved surface: hairlines,
        plate numbers, registration marks, and a single copper line. The structure is
        brutalist; the surface is neoclassical. Neither is allowed to become decoration.
      </p>
      <p>
        All diagrams are drawn as SVG. There are no stock photographs and no generated
        imagery. The armillary and the seal are constructed from circles, axes, and
        ticks — the same geometry that gives the site its name.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="page-section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <aside class="split__aside">
      <span class="eyebrow">II / Type</span>
      <h2>Three voices.</h2>
    </aside>
    <div class="split__body">
      <dl class="ledger">
        <div class="ledger__row">
          <dt>Display</dt>
          <dd>Bodoni Moda — high-contrast serif for the name, headlines, and plates.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="ledger__row">
          <dt>Text</dt>
          <dd>Newsreader — a quieter serif for running copy and long-form notes.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="ledger__row">
          <dt>Technical</dt>
          <dd>IBM Plex Mono — labels, coordinates, metadata, and the margin.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="ledger__row">
          <dt>License</dt>
          <dd>All three are open-source typefaces, self-hosted as WOFF2.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

